hase: creates the structured artifacts (proposal, specs, design, tasks) |\n219:  worker: codex                    # or claude\n220:  scrutiny_validator: claude\n221:  usertest_validator: claude\n223:  adversarial_reviewer_b: claude\n224:  demo_video: claude\n227:The default uses Codex for workers and one of the two independent code reviewers, and Claude for everything else. You can set any role to either engin [... omitted end of long line]\n257:This is a separate skill, not a flag on `/mission`. It reads the files on disk, figures out exactly where the mission was interrupted -- including tas [... omitted end of long line]\n281:The first version was hand-written during a `/grill-me` session that produced the design decisions and shared vocabulary. The second version was built [... omitted end of long line]\n286:- [Matt Pocock skills talk](docs/reference_pocock_talk.md) -- design alignment, ubiquitous language, and TDD patterns\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
